From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Schwering <schwering@google.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:44:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] [Autofill] Clamp coordinates to all ancestor
 RenderWidgetHostViews

Previously, Lift() only intersected field bounds with the sending
frame's own RenderWidgetHostView bounds. For a nested cross-process
iframe, the parent frame's renderer controls the inner frame's declared
local_frame_size, so an outer cross-site iframe could inflate the inner
cross-site iframe's view bounds via CSS and position the Autofill popup
outside the outer iframe's bounds.

This CL transforms the rectangle to root coordinates first and then
clamps it against the root-space bounds of the sending frame's view and
all ancestor RenderWidgetHostViews.

TAG=agy
CONV=f3ec8eff-4abc-4c8b-88f9-0fd6d4f49938

